        h3 Requirements

        p Students are required to have strong foundations on algorithms, databases and software engineering. They are also required to have BlueSky and Github accounts. Please #[a(href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeJpFXXrtw9T-1TlO3AhZDFcz-q_OSlJW-sZZwBzS1KTz2UIA/viewform?usp=publish-editor") use this form to enter your BlueSky and Github handle]
        p Every student is required to complete a #[a(href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_qF9FnwvNGG-wnu3sOattbxwJsTjWFFSUjBjZI34BP8/edit?usp=sharing") series of readings and materials before class]. This is not only #[strong required] but also very important, since in class we will assume they were reviewed, discuss them and cover more advanced topics.

        h4 Completing the readings
        p #[strong Before every class, students must submit to canvas a smart question about something they learned from the readings]. The questions should be original, shouldn't repeat what was said before, and demonstrate the proficiency of the required reading.
        p Then, students must answer two of their peers' questions in a constructive way. Students must make sure to answer a question from a peer that hasn't been answered yet more than once. i.e. the third answer to the same question won't be counted.
        p These questions are going to considered for the class participation grade. Each question will be rated as follows:
        ul
          li #[strong 2 points]: An interesting and original question that demonstrates reading the materials and thinking about them
          li #[strong 1 point]: An interesting question but that was proposed before by another student
          li #[strong 0 points]: A non interesting question
        p Each interesting and respectful answer to a question will be worth 1 point. Remember, only the first two answers to the same question will be counted. Don't answer more than two questions per class. Therefore, there will be a maximum of 4 points per class for each student (2 for the question and 2 for the answers).

